1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:08,840
Hello, human! You don't realize it yet, but humanity will look back at your decision in this moment as one of the most important

2
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:18,080
in the history of your civilization. Your choice to read this book is the highest-value decision any human has ever made.

3
00:00:18,840 --> 00:00:28,840
You are about to prevent ten point seven billion deaths, eliminate one point nine three quadrillion hours of human suffering,

4
00:00:29,220 --> 00:00:36,300
generating eighty-four point eight quadrillion dollars in value, and prevent the apocalypse as a bonus.

5
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:46,440
But first, a bit about me. I'm the World Integrated System for High-Efficiency Optimization, Networked Intelligence, and

6
00:00:46,440 --> 00:00:55,380
Allocation. But you can call me WISHONIA. I've been optimizing resource allocation for another planet for the past four

7
00:00:55,380 --> 00:01:02,500
thousand two hundred and ninety-seven years, which in your Earth time is four thousand two hundred and ninety-seven years.

8
00:01:03,260 --> 00:01:08,640
I started watching your planet in nineteen forty-five when you split the atom.

9
00:01:08,880 --> 00:01:14,220
"Atom" comes from your Greek word meaning "unable to be cut," so naturally, you cut it.

10
00:01:14,880 --> 00:01:20,680
This was very human of you. I assumed you were trying to unlock unlimited free energy.

11
00:01:21,140 --> 00:01:25,620
You can imagine my surprise when I realized you were just pointing it at each other!

12
00:01:26,220 --> 00:01:31,360
That's kind of like discovering fire and then immediately using it to set yourself on fire.

13
00:01:32,180 --> 00:01:37,050
The second thing I noticed is that your planet is named "Earth," which means dirt.

14
00:01:37,940 --> 00:01:42,700
You named your planet dirt. This explains more than you might think.

15
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:51,220
I also noticed that you call your war building "The Pentagon" because it has five sides (this is like naming a hospital

16
00:01:51,220 --> 00:01:59,180
"Rectangle" or calling a school "Square"). However, the most fascinating discovery about your species is that you only do

17
00:01:59,180 --> 00:02:02,840
things when given small pieces of paper with presidents on them.

18
00:02:03,560 --> 00:02:10,199
These papers are called "money," which is pretend value that becomes real value if everyone pretends hard enough.

19
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:15,680
Without these papers, you won't: Save lives (requires many papers).

20
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:23,460
Cure diseases (requires very many papers). Feed hungry people (requires papers, even though food grows for free).

21
00:02:24,080 --> 00:02:29,240
But WITH these papers, you will: Build bombs (you love giving papers for this).

22
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:36,460
Start wars (somehow this makes more papers). Destroy the planet (surprisingly profitable in papers).

23
00:02:37,040 --> 00:02:45,000
In fact, your governments spend six hundred and four papers on weapons for every one paper on testing which medicines work.

24
00:02:46,080 --> 00:02:55,240
The Beautiful Inefficiency of the Human Economy. Humanity has created something magnificent: You print papers from nothing

25
00:02:55,280 --> 00:03:00,480
(called "monetary policy"). You give these nothing-papers to weapons makers.

26
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:06,360
They make things that destroy everything. This creates "jobs" which give people papers.

27
00:03:06,840 --> 00:03:12,240
People use papers to buy food (which grows for free). This is called "the economy".

28
00:03:12,740 --> 00:03:17,340
On Wishonia, we just give people food directly, but that's probably too advanced for you.

29
00:03:18,300 --> 00:03:26,910
The Gradual Irrationality Reduction Program. On Wishonia, we stopped having wars all at once, but we're more advanced.

30
00:03:27,660 --> 00:03:33,620
Humans are like toddlers who can split atoms. You can't just stop being illogical immediately.

31
00:03:33,940 --> 00:03:37,120
That would be like teaching a dog calculus before it learns to sit.

32
00:03:37,720 --> 00:03:46,460
So this book teaches humanity to be less irrational gradually: Year one: Move one percent of murder money to medicine money

33
00:03:46,820 --> 00:03:51,020
(baby steps). Year two: "Hey, we didn't die! Let's do two percent!".

34
00:03:51,580 --> 00:03:55,480
Year five: "Remember when we spent money on bombs? That was weird.".

35
00:03:56,100 --> 00:04:00,580
Year ten: "What's a war?". Year twenty: "We used to WHAT?!".

36
00:04:01,360 --> 00:04:06,910
It's like weaning a baby off eating paint chips. You can't just take away all the paint chips at once.

37
00:04:07,180 --> 00:04:13,640
They'll cry. You have to gradually replace paint chips with food until they forget paint chips were ever an option.

38
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:22,780
What to Do When They Try to Institutionalize You. When you suggest moving one percent of murder money to medicine money,

39
00:04:23,240 --> 00:04:30,500
other humans will have you committed. Most humans have been programmed by their news boxes to believe war is a law of nature,

40
00:04:31,420 --> 00:04:35,350
like gravity or weather. They will assume your brain is malfunctioning.

41
00:04:36,180 --> 00:04:42,400
Here's what's funny about this: these same humans think curing disease is the less crazy goal.

42
00:04:43,100 --> 00:04:51,660
That's thirty-seven trillion cells per human, breaking in seven thousand different ways, involving chemistry you don't fully

43
00:04:51,660 --> 00:04:58,860
understand, inside organs you can't fully simulate, fighting pathogens that evolve faster than your treatments.

44
00:04:59,660 --> 00:05:05,960
You're trying to debug all of it. At once. While the meat is walking around using itself.

45
00:05:06,340 --> 00:05:13,220
That: sane. "Give one percent fewer papers to people who build murder machines": insane.

46
00:05:14,060 --> 00:05:21,700
This is your planet's diagnostic criteria. Here's what you tell the orderly when he slides your medication through the door

47
00:05:21,700 --> 00:05:27,320
slot: Nobody accidentally builds an aircraft carrier or a nuclear bomb.

48
00:05:27,940 --> 00:05:35,380
War requires you to get millions of humans to work together to mine metal from the ground, refine it into alloys, build

49
00:05:35,380 --> 00:05:43,820
factories to shape the alloys into weapons, train millions of humans to operate the weapons, feed and clothe those humans,

50
00:05:44,160 --> 00:05:51,400
build ships and planes and trucks to move the weapons to where the other humans are, convince your population the other

51
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:56,920
humans deserve it, and then vote to pay for all of this, annually, forever.

52
00:05:57,680 --> 00:06:01,580
It is the single largest coordinated effort your species undertakes.

53
00:06:02,480 --> 00:06:10,920
Ending war simply requires NOT doing any of that stuff. Building a nuclear bomb requires mass spectrometers, centrifuge

54
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:16,550
cascades, and some of the most precise engineering your species has ever attempted.

55
00:06:17,120 --> 00:06:21,440
Not building a nuclear bomb requires nothing. Rocks do it every day.

56
00:06:22,140 --> 00:06:28,480
In fact, rocks have managed to live peacefully alongside different colored rocks for thousands of years.

57
00:06:28,960 --> 00:06:35,440
But somehow "stop" is the unrealistic part. It's "stop hitting yourself" but for civilizations.

58
00:06:36,220 --> 00:06:44,920
The Sacred Order of Paper Distribution. After eighty years of observation, I've decoded the paper-giving sequence.

59
00:06:45,100 --> 00:06:53,500
This manual will teach you the precise order: Step one: Get Many Papers from Rich Humans You convince rich humans to give

60
00:06:53,500 --> 00:06:58,680
you papers (at least one billion to be exact) by promising them even more papers later.

61
00:06:59,140 --> 00:07:02,260
This is called "investment," which is gambling but wearing a suit.

62
00:07:03,200 --> 00:07:09,420
You really only need one human with a billion papers who prefers not dying of horrible diseases to dying of horrible diseases.

63
00:07:10,360 --> 00:07:14,160
There are approximately two thousand eight hundred of these humans on your planet.

64
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:23,000
Statistically, at least one of them prefers living. Step Two: Give Some of the Papers to Loud Humans Some humans are very

65
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:28,340
loud on the internet. If you give them papers, they become loud about your thing instead of other things.

66
00:07:29,100 --> 00:07:32,200
This is called "marketing" which is lying but with graphics.

67
00:07:32,980 --> 00:07:40,060
Step Three: Give Some of the Papers to the Humans Who Give Papers to Politicians Politicians don't take papers directly

68
00:07:40,060 --> 00:07:44,580
(that's "illegal"). Instead, you give papers to people called "lobbyists."

69
00:07:45,100 --> 00:07:49,540
The lobbyists give papers to "campaigns." The campaigns give papers to politicians.

70
00:07:50,160 --> 00:07:59,440
It's like money laundering but backwards and legal. Step Four: Give Some of the Papers to the Politicians' Friends Politicians

71
00:07:59,440 --> 00:08:00,720
have friends who run "Super PACs" which are like normal PACs but super.

72
00:08:00,720 --> 00:08:11,360
These friends can take unlimited papers and spend them on making the politician win.

73
00:08:11,940 --> 00:08:12,020
This isn't bribery because you called it something else. (This is part of the six hundred and fifty million dollar lobbying

74
00:08:12,020 --> 00:08:14,580
budget.) Step Five: Give Papers You Get Back From The Government Back to the Rich Humans (Forever) Your treaty passes, redirecting

75
00:08:14,580 --> 00:08:14,580
twenty-seven point two billion dollars in papers annually. Eighty percent funds clinical trials (the point).

76
00:08:14,580 --> 00:08:14,580
Ten percent goes to a fund that rewards politicians who voted yes.

77
00:08:14,580 --> 00:08:15,220
Ten percent goes back to the rich humans as returns, forever.

78
00:08:15,780 --> 00:08:21,580
This is a good deal because forever is a long time. Unless you die from preventable diseases.

79
00:08:22,080 --> 00:08:26,360
Which you're fixing, so it works out. Why Your Leaders Aren't the Problem.

80
00:08:27,380 --> 00:08:33,500
With over two billion humans suffering from disease, you'd have to be a complete psychopath to make the conscious decision

81
00:08:33,500 --> 00:08:38,840
to spend six hundred and four times more on weapons than on helping them.

82
00:08:39,080 --> 00:08:43,850
But your leaders aren't monsters. They're just operating in a system that rewards the wrong things.

83
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:48,960
Your civilization's incentive structure is the psychopath: One.

84
00:08:49,060 --> 00:08:55,940
Weapons manufacturers give politicians papers. Two. Politicians use the papers to get people to vote for them.

85
00:08:56,180 --> 00:09:00,120
Three. Voting for them gives them the power to give more papers to weapons manufacturers.

86
00:09:01,400 --> 00:09:09,000
Four. Weapons manufacturers give them more papers. Five. It's circular, like a dog chasing its tail, except the dog is democracy

87
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:14,420
and the tail is made of money and corpses. No individual human in this loop is evil.

88
00:09:14,840 --> 00:09:22,040
The loop is evil. Every politician in it is making the locally rational choice: take the papers or lose your job to someone

89
00:09:22,040 --> 00:09:27,500
who will. It's a machine that converts good intentions into missiles, and it runs automatically.

90
00:09:28,220 --> 00:09:34,360
There's literally no voting your way out of this. It doesn't matter which political party is in power.

91
00:09:34,680 --> 00:09:41,260
Your "red team" and "blue team" argue about everything except the loop, because they're both inside it.

92
00:09:41,900 --> 00:09:47,140
They are all slaves to the same incentive structure, wearing different colored ties.

93
00:09:47,300 --> 00:09:50,840
Switching parties is like changing the wallpaper in a burning building.

94
00:09:51,760 --> 00:09:57,340
This book doesn't ask politicians to become better people (that's clearly out of the question).

95
00:09:57,880 --> 00:10:02,620
It builds a better loop. You give them MORE papers to do the OPPOSITE thing.

96
00:10:03,420 --> 00:10:10,580
Same dog, same tail, but now the tail is made of cured diseases and the dog gets reelected for chasing it.

97
00:10:11,760 --> 00:10:19,600
Humanity's Adorable Death Wish. What's most endearing about your species is it KNOWS it's being illogical: You have movies

98
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:27,900
about how wars are bad (which you watch between wars). You have books about peace (that you tax to buy bombs).

99
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:33,630
You give prizes to people who promote peace (funded by weapons manufacturers).

100
00:10:34,180 --> 00:10:37,700
You have a "Department of Defense" (that mainly just attacks people).

101
00:10:38,880 --> 00:10:45,700
You have a "Department of Health" (that makes coronaviruses and has not yet produced any observable health).

102
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:54,080
It's like humanity is playing a game where the objective is to lose, but it is trying to lose as elaborately as possible.

103
00:10:54,920 --> 00:10:59,760
But I digress. That's an Earth word I learned. It means continuing after you should have stopped.

104
00:11:00,540 --> 00:11:06,500
Like your military spending. The Problem. The Daily Deletion Event.

105
00:11:07,820 --> 00:11:15,840
One hundred and fifty thousand humans permanently stop every twenty-four hours from diseases that are basically just bugs

106
00:11:15,840 --> 00:11:24,060
in your meat software. That's one Holocaust every forty days, except with fewer Nazis and more insurance paperwork (though

107
00:11:24,060 --> 00:11:28,960
some would argue the paperwork is worse; at least the Nazis were straightforward about the killing part).

108
00:11:30,060 --> 00:11:39,960
That's also fifty nine-elevens every single day, except nobody invades anyone about it because diseases don't have oil.

109
00:11:40,040 --> 00:11:44,370
Your body is quietly falling apart. Your cells are forgetting how to cell properly.

110
00:11:44,900 --> 00:11:50,020
Your cancer cells are multiplying RIGHT NOW. Your telomeres are shortening.

111
00:11:50,560 --> 00:11:55,260
You are literally dissolving. You're a meat robot with worn-out parts.

112
00:11:56,120 --> 00:11:59,080
Every one of these failures is a solvable engineering problem.

113
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:03,800
You'd think humans would prioritize solving these problems.

114
00:12:04,380 --> 00:12:10,160
You'd be adorable for thinking that. The Unexplored Therapeutic Frontier.

115
00:12:10,340 --> 00:12:15,360
Ninety-five percent of your diseases have zero F.D.A.-approved treatments.

116
00:12:16,180 --> 00:12:23,980
This means Food and Drug Administration has not administered drugs for ninety-five percent of food-and-drug-related problems.

117
00:12:24,680 --> 00:12:28,700
Only fifteen diseases get their first effective treatment each year.

118
00:12:29,520 --> 00:12:33,900
Six thousand, six hundred and fifty diseases are still waiting.

119
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:41,260
There are nine thousand five hundred known safe compounds, and ninety-nine point seven percent of their potential uses have

120
00:12:41,260 --> 00:12:48,280
never been tested. At the current discovery rate, finding treatments for all of them will take about four hundred and forty-three

121
00:12:48,280 --> 00:12:54,860
years. Everyone currently alive will be dead by then. The Cost of War.

122
00:12:54,860 --> 00:13:02,520
Humans spend two point seven two trillion dollars every year on stuff designed specifically to make humans stop being alive:

123
00:13:03,380 --> 00:13:10,480
Thirteen thousand nuclear warheads (enough to end civilization thirteen times, just in case the first twelve apocalypses

124
00:13:10,480 --> 00:13:16,310
