125
00:13:16,780 --> 00:13:22,210
Space Force (to fight the zero aliens attacking you). And some kind of earthquake machine (probably).

126
00:13:23,300 --> 00:13:28,160
Government spending on clinical trials: six hundred and four times less than military spending.

127
00:13:29,440 --> 00:13:32,920
Your chance of dying from terrorism: one in thirty million.

128
00:13:33,480 --> 00:13:41,040
Your chance of dying from disease: one hundred percent. If cancer had oil reserves, you would have cured it by two thousand

129
00:13:41,040 --> 00:13:49,280
and three. Instead, you spent the repair money on murder tubes that cost more than countries and submarines that hide underwater,

130
00:13:49,640 --> 00:13:54,100
as if that's somehow useful when you live on land. The F.D.A.

131
00:13:54,320 --> 00:14:02,520
is Unsafe and Ineffective. Even the money you DO spend on medicine is mostly wasted, because the system that approves treatments

132
00:14:02,520 --> 00:14:10,080
is a smoke detector that works by mail. Vioxx killed an estimated thirty-eight thousand to fifty-five thousand people from

133
00:14:10,080 --> 00:14:16,540
heart attacks. The F.D.A. approved it. When patients started dying, someone filled out a P.D.F.

134
00:14:16,800 --> 00:14:25,760
form. A P.D.F. Then they faxed it. (Yes, this is how your system works in the twenty-first century.) Then a human read it.

135
00:14:26,140 --> 00:14:30,480
Five years and tens of thousands of corpses later, someone noticed a pattern.

136
00:14:31,300 --> 00:14:39,420
This is your safety system. Your National Institutes of Health, the agency nominally responsible for finding cures, spends

137
00:14:39,420 --> 00:14:44,380
three point three percent of its budget on clinical trials (see N.I.H.

138
00:14:44,380 --> 00:14:50,900
fails to institute health). The other about ninety-seven percent goes to basic research, administration, and buildings.

139
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:55,460
It's like a fire department that spends three percent of its budget on water.

140
00:14:56,340 --> 00:15:03,120
Then there's a eight point two years delay between proving a drug is safe and letting dying humans take it.

141
00:15:03,780 --> 00:15:08,360
The drug passed the safety test. Everyone agrees it won't kill you.

142
00:15:08,560 --> 00:15:15,500
But you still can't have it because a committee needs to spend eight point two years making sure it works well enough.

143
00:15:15,660 --> 00:15:22,160
You'd volunteer for the trials that would answer that question faster, but so would one point zero eight billion other patients,

144
00:15:22,640 --> 00:15:27,580
and the current system has one million nine hundred thousand patient-per-year slots.

145
00:15:27,580 --> 00:15:30,780
That's a participation rate of zero point zero six percent.

146
00:15:31,880 --> 00:15:38,440
It's like a lifeguard who confirms the life preserver floats, then locks it in a cabinet for years to study its buoyancy

147
00:15:38,440 --> 00:15:42,800
profile while a billion people drown in line for the two available life jackets.

148
00:15:43,820 --> 00:15:52,060
Your regulatory system can make two mistakes: approve a bad drug (Type One error), or block a good drug (Type Two error).

149
00:15:52,960 --> 00:15:57,460
Your F.D.A. is terrified of the first mistake and completely ignores the second.

150
00:15:58,380 --> 00:16:06,800
I calculated the ratio: for every one person protected from a dangerous drug, three thousand and seventy people die waiting

151
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:14,660
for a safe one that's locked in the approval cabinet. Even if you assume a Thalidomide-scale catastrophe happens during

152
00:16:14,900 --> 00:16:22,680
post-phase one efficacy testing every single year (even though it wouldn't because Phase One safety testing actually caught

153
00:16:22,680 --> 00:16:31,400
it anyway), the deaths from just the efficacy delay still outnumber the deaths from bad drugs by three thousand and seventy

154
00:16:31,400 --> 00:16:36,520
to one. Your safety system's main product is dead patients.

155
00:16:37,480 --> 00:16:43,580
The good news: You already know how to fix this. The bad news: It requires you to do something.

156
00:16:44,660 --> 00:16:50,820
The weird news: You'll get rich doing it. The Solution. A one percent Treaty.

157
00:16:51,760 --> 00:16:59,340
This is going to sound crazy. But you're going to use those papers to persuade the leader of every country on Earth to simultaneously

158
00:16:59,340 --> 00:17:03,540
redirect one percent of its military budget to clinical trials.

159
00:17:04,319 --> 00:17:13,960
That's it. That's the treaty. After the craziness objection, the second objection every human has: "But if we cut our military

160
00:17:13,960 --> 00:17:21,160
budget, our enemies will invade us!" Everyone cuts one percent at the same time.

161
00:17:21,760 --> 00:17:27,680
If every country reduces by one percent simultaneously, the balance of power doesn't change.

162
00:17:28,359 --> 00:17:35,580
Nobody becomes more vulnerable. Nobody gains an advantage. You all just have one percent fewer missiles pointed at you,

163
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:41,280
which you will not notice because you currently have enough to kill everyone twenty times over.

164
00:17:42,520 --> 00:17:51,660
two point six nine trillion dollars is still enough to murder every man, woman, and child on Earth twenty times, which should

165
00:17:51,660 --> 00:17:56,100
